; EdSharp.inix -- OPTIONAL layered configuration (a superset of EdSharp.ini).
;
; This template ships in the program folder for reference. EdSharp looks for an
; active EdSharp.inix next to your user EdSharp.ini (in EdSharp's data folder).
; If that file exists, any [Section] Key entry here OVERRIDES the same entry in
; EdSharp.ini; anything not listed falls back to EdSharp.ini unchanged. With no
; active EdSharp.inix, or with every line commented as below, EdSharp behaves
; exactly as it always has.
;
; Over classic .ini, the .inix format adds:
;   - verbatim multi-line values,
;   - an implicit [Global] section for keys above the first [Section] header,
;   - order-preserving round-trip (keys keep their order when rewritten).
;
; Lines beginning with a semicolon are comments. To activate an override,
; copy this file next to your EdSharp.ini, then uncomment and edit entries:
;
; [Data]
; Compiler=Python
; 
; --- Default text encoding (Options section) ---------------------------
; YieldEncoding controls the encoding EdSharp reads and writes for text
; documents. Leave it blank (the default) and EdSharp auto-detects on open
; -- a byte-order mark wins, otherwise the content is examined -- and writes
; UTF-8 with BOM (utf8b) when the encoding is otherwise undetermined or for a
; new file. The detected encoding is remembered per document, so Save keeps a
; file in the encoding it came in with. Set a value to force one encoding for
; both open and save. Recognized values:
;   utf8b   UTF-8 with BOM (the default behavior when blank)
;   utf8n   UTF-8 without BOM (also selects Unix line breaks)
;   utf16   UTF-16 little-endian (also: utf16le, unicode)
;   utf16be UTF-16 big-endian
;   ansi    the system ANSI code page
;   <number or name>  any code page number or .NET encoding name, e.g. 1252
;
; [Options]
; YieldEncoding=
; 
; --- Compiler settings (Compilers section and per-compiler sections) ----
; The Compile command (Control+F5) runs the current compiler/interpreter, jumps
; to the first reported error, and speaks the (optionally abbreviated) output.
; With NO compiler configured, EdSharp now compiles a C# (.cs) file out of the
; box using the latest available .NET Framework C# compiler (Roslyn csc.exe if
; installed, otherwise the framework csc that always ships with .NET), and jumps
; to the first error -- so the built-in default needs no setup.
; 
; A compiler is normally one tilde-delimited value in the [Compilers] section:
;   <name>=CompileCommand~JumpPosition~AbbreviateOutput~NavigatePart~QuotePrefix~ExtensionDefault~GoToEnvironment
; where JumpPosition is a regex whose first number is the error line and second
; (if any) is the column. That packing is brittle if a field itself contains a
; tilde. More solidly, define a section named "Compiler <name>" with one key per
; setting; its keys override the packed fields when you pick that compiler. The
; .inix format keeps each value verbatim, so regexes need no escaping:
; 
; [Compiler C#]
; CompileCommand="csc.exe" /nologo "%SourceLong%" 2>&1
; JumpPosition=\(\d+,\d+\)
; AbbreviateOutput=\r
; NavigatePart=^( |\t)*((public)|(private)|(internal)|(protected)|(static)|(void)|(class)|(struct))[^;]*?\{ *$
; QuotePrefix=//
; ExtensionDefault=cs
; 
; --- Document-to-text converters via 2htm (Import / Export sections) ------
; The bundled 2htm utility (Convert\2htm\2htm.exe, by Jamal Mazrui) extracts
; readable plain text from many formats -- .docx .doc .rtf .odt .pdf .xlsx
; .xls .pptx .ppt .csv .html .htm .md .json .txt -- in one tool.  The new
; default EdSharp.ini already routes the document-to-text conversions through
; it (via Convert\any2txt.cmd, which runs 2htm with -p for plain text).  This
; retires GetText.exe, which hung on modern Windows, and the Office COM text
; converters (WdVert/XlVert/PpVert) and htm2txt.exe for text extraction.
; 
; If your data-folder EdSharp.ini still has the OLD converter lines (an
; existing install keeps its own copy), copy this EdSharp.inix next to that
; EdSharp.ini and UNCOMMENT the lines below to switch over immediately --
; non-destructively, since EdSharp reads .inix entries in preference to .ini.
; (xls2csv / xlsx2csv are left on XlVert because 2htm cannot output CSV.)
; 
; [Import]
; doc2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; html2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; ppt2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; pptx2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; xls2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; xlsx2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; hlp2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; wpd2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; 
; [Export]
; html2txt=%ProgDir%\Convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
; 
; --- Conversion on open (ViewLevels) ----------------------------------------
; When a file is opened from outside the editor (Explorer, "Open with", the
; command line, or Recent Files) EdSharp opens it raw, except binary/document
; formats (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, PDF, EPUB, WordPerfect, WinHelp, RTF),
; which are converted.  No text format (.md, .json, .htm, .inix, .csv, .rst,
; .brl, .brf, source code, etc.) is auto-converted.  Control+O always opens
; raw; Control+Shift+O always converts.
; ViewLevels overrides this per extension: 0 = open raw, 1 = convert.  It is a
; single space-separated list.  Uncomment and edit to taste, for example to
; back-translate braille on open or to open Word files raw:
; 
; [Options]
; ViewLevels="brl:1 brf:1 docx:0"
